#X text 1300 170 C-8: select 1's reject carries the mode itself \, so t b b turns it into the beat row's two bangs., f 40;
#X text 2100 1420 Mode 1 is the drum page: the beat row gives way \, and each row of the layout table paints one cell. A step is dim when off \, and on in four steps of one palette hue by its velocity \, 8 for the softest up to 11 for the loudest \, and white under the playhead. The selected velocity and pad are 9 \, the rest dim. Row 4 and the bottom-right 4x4 are in no row \, so they stay dark., f 60;
#X restore 900 330 pd regions;
#X text 900 430 The fill is the clear: every frame writes all 108 cells first. t b b f stores the color \, resets the counter \, then runs the loop., f 50;
#X text 900 600 The counter reset goes into the cold inlet off the rightmost outlet \, so a loop never starts where the last one stopped., f 50;
